    "summary": "`uncbv`: archive extraction is vulnerable to path traversal (zip-slip)",
    "details": "### Summary\n\n`uncbv extract` writes each archive entry to `output_dir.join(entry_filename)` using the filename stored in the archive with no check for `..` components or absolute paths. A malicious `.cbv` / `.cbz` archive whose entry name contains `../` (or an absolute path) can therefore cause files to be written outside the output directory chosen by the user. This is a \"zip-slip\" / directory-traversal arbitrary file write (CWE-22).",
